# Lint and audit tools that CI installs (.github/workflows/pylint.yml).
# requirements-dev.txt is autogenerated from this file: pip-compile requirements-dev.in
# Compile with Python 3.12, the oldest supported version: the header records the
# interpreter, and Dependabot compiles with the one recorded there.
#
# No "-c requirements.txt" constraint: Dependabot orders its pip-compile runs by
# "-r" lines only, so the constraint would hold a shared package (certifi, idna,
# ...) at its old pin and make Dependabot's update of it unresolvable. CI installs
# both lockfiles in one pip call, so a pin that differs between them fails there.
bandit
pip-audit
pylint
# cyclonedx-python-lib (via pip-audit) needs typing-extensions>=4.6,<5 on Python < 3.13
# only. Listed so the pin survives a compile on 3.13, which would otherwise drop it
# and leave the 3.12 CI job with an unpinned copy.
typing-extensions<5
